BANKING FRAUD ANALYTICS PROJECT

Project Title: Banking Risk & Fraud Intelligence Analytics System

1. Project Introduction

The main objective of this project is to analyse credit card transactions and identify fraudulent transactions using Python, SQL and data analysis techniques.

2. Dataset Description

I used the Credit Card Fraud Detection dataset for this project. I took the dataset from kaggle.

The dataset contains the following columns:

- Time – Transaction time in seconds.
- Amount – Transaction amount.
- V1 to V28 – Transformed transaction features.
- Class – 0 represents genuine transactions and 1 represents fraudulent transactions.

3. Tools and Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas
- MySQL
- Excel
- VS Code

4. Python Analysis Completed

1. Data Cleaning
2. Basic Data Analysis
3. Statistical Analysis
4. Fraud Pattern Analysis
5. Feature Correlation Analysis
6. Average Transaction Amount Comparison
7. Transaction Amount Range Analysis

5. Key Findings

- Average genuine transaction amount: 88.41
- Average fraudulent transaction amount: 123.87
- Fraudulent transactions have a higher average amount than genuine transactions in this dataset.
- Statistical analysis was performed to identify unusual transaction amounts.
- Fraud and genuine transactions were compared using the Class column.

6. Project Conclusion

This project helped me understand how Python and SQL can be used to analyse banking transaction data.
By performing data cleaning, statistical analysis and fraud pattern analysis, I identified differences between genuine and fraudulent transactions.
The project helped me improve my practical knowledge of data analysis and understand how data can support fraud detection.